# Files removed from the sparse tree after our own sparse/ has been overlaid.
#
# droid-configs-device/droid-configs.inc builds the tree by copying, in order,
# the submodule's sparse trees and then ours, and applies this list last:
#
#     copy_files_from %{dcd_path}/sparse
#     delete_files tmp/droid-config.files delete_file_%{rpm_device}.list 1
#
# One path per line, absolute within the image. '#' comments and blank lines
# are ignored.
#
# /etc/ofono/binder.conf
#   Comes from the mer-hybris/droid-hal-configs submodule and declares
#   "ExpectSlots = slot1" -- a single SIM. karatep is dual-SIM, and this
#   adaptation configures both slots itself in sparse/etc/ofono/
#   ril_subscription.conf ([ril_0] transport=binder:name=slot1, [ril_1]
#   transport=binder:name=slot2), so upstream's single-slot file has to go.
#
#   This was previously done by deleting the file inside the submodule's
#   working tree. That is an unmanaged edit to an upstream repository: it does
#   not survive `repo sync`, it exists on no other machine, and it silently
#   changes what the build produces. This list is the mechanism
#   droid-configs.inc provides for exactly this case.
#
#   If it ever turns out the binder plugin is the right one for this device,
#   the fix is to delete this list and drop ril_subscription.conf -- not to
#   touch the submodule.
/etc/ofono/binder.conf
